meta {
  name: 12c. Cleanup - Delete POSTGIS DataSink
  type: http
  seq: 37
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/datasets/:dataSetId/datasinks/:id
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  dataSetId: {{sagaDataSetId}}
  id: {{sagaPostgisDataSinkId}}
}

tests {
  test("Provisioned POSTGIS DataSink refused", function() {
    const status = res.getStatus();
    // 409=provisioned by the release in step 8, 204=never provisioned (release saga failed),
    // 404=already gone, 400=sagaPostgisDataSinkId never set (aborted run)
    expect(status === 409 || status === 204 || status === 404 || status === 400).to.be.true;
    if (status === 409) {
      expect(res.getBody().type).to.equal("urn:civitas:error:RESOURCE_IN_USE");
    }
  });
}

docs {
  **Saga step 12c** — Delete the POSTGIS DataSink (refused).

  The release in step 8 provisioned the DataSink created in step 4d. A provisioned DataSink keeps its storage after an unrelease, and only the DataSet teardown removes that storage, so a standalone delete is refused with `409` even though the DataSet is a draft again. The DataSink goes together with the DataSet in step 13.

  **Expected Response:** 409 Conflict (`RESOURCE_IN_USE`). 204 if the release saga failed and nothing was provisioned. 404 if already deleted. 400 if `sagaPostgisDataSinkId` is not set (first run / aborted earlier).

  **System Impact:**

  | Layer | Effect |
  |---|---|
  | Backend | — (DataSink record kept) |
  | Config Adapter | — |
}
